Third-party data and attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product uses the OpenLimbTT transtibial residual limb shape model
(Sunderland, Sobey, Bramley et al., 2025), from the repository
abel-research/OpenLimbTT (https://github.com/abel-research/OpenLimbTT).

  - OpenLimbTT *data* (mean mesh and PCA modes) is licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0.
  - OpenLimbTT *code* is licensed MIT.

The OpenLimbTT data is downloaded at runtime (see scripts/fetch_openlimb.py)
and is NOT redistributed in this repository. Any limb or socket mesh generated
from the OpenLimbTT model is a derivative of CC-BY-SA-4.0 data and, if
distributed, must carry that licence and this attribution.

Citation:
  F. E. Sunderland, A. J. Sobey, J. L. Bramley, et al. (2025). OpenLimbTT, a
  transtibial residual limb shape model for prosthetics simulation and design.
  Data-Centric Engineering, 6:e39.

The rectification parameterisation defaults are grounded in published clinical
literature, principally:
  - Dickinson et al. (2024), Frontiers in Rehabilitation Sciences, 5:1354069.
  - Convery & Buis (2003), Prosthetics and Orthotics International, 27(3).

Full provenance, licensing notes, and the exact assumptions behind the default
values are documented in docs/SOURCES.md.
